Hi all,

I have a MSOM and iI am trying to incorporate code to calculate a Bayesian p-value as a goodness of fit test into my existing MSOM code in JAGS. The original code/model ran fine, but I am getting a syntax/parsing error when trying to incorporate code to calculate the Bayesian P-value. Specifically the error is: "Error parsing model file: syntax error on line 15 near "," ". In R, this is line: "mu.p[i, k] <- (p[i, k] * z[i, k], nOcc[i])". It would seem to me like it's having an error with the comma before n0cc[i] (which incorporates differences in the number of survey replicates per site) but the model runs fine when the code to calculate the p-value is not incorporated, so I'm a little stumped. I'm following along with code from Bajaru et al. 2019 <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1616504719300667> which uses chi2 disrepancies. It is similar to code from Tobler et al. 2015 <https://besjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/1365-2664.12399?casa_token=6ewPxA4kcScAAAAA%3AVLf-v3eJAlKDs2RlyG0QfJRb37TWPOPjiSQUZdBuYS3XXjOGDfkAVRW2foG3ACgwTdskQstNeLvKWvQ>  which uses Pearson residuals.

Any insight on what might be happening would be appreciated! I'll include my original code (which runs) below, and the updated code with the new sections to calculate the Bayesian P-value below it.

Original code:

model{
  for(k in 1:M){  # Loop through species
    w[k] ~ dbern(omega)

    # Likelihood
    for(i in 1:nSites) {
       # Ecological model
      logit(psi[i, k]) <- b0[k] + bFor[k] * forest[i] +
          bFor2[k] * forest2[i]
       z[i, k] ~ dbern(psi[i, k] * w[k])
       # Observation model
       logit(p[i, k]) <- a0[k] + aTrail[k] * trail[i]
       y[i, k] ~ dbin(p[i, k] * z[i, k], nOcc[i])
    }

    # Priors (species level)/species heterogeneity
    b0[k] ~ dnorm(mu.b0, tau.b0)
    mu.eta[k] <- mu.a0 + rho * sd.a0/sd.b0 *
        (b0[k] - mu.b0)
    a0[k] ~ dnorm(mu.eta[k], tau.eta)

    bFor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.bforest, tau.bforest)
    bFor2[k] ~ dnorm(mu.bforest2, tau.bforest2)

    aTrail[k]~ dnorm(mu.atrail, tau.atrail)
  }

  # Hyperpriors (community level)
  omega ~ dbeta(0.001, 1) #Link's scale prior

## for occupancy
  mu.b0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.b0 ~ dt(0, 1, 1)T(0,)
  tau.b0 <- 1/sd.b0^2

  mu.bforest ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.bforest ~ dt(0, 1, 1)T(0,)
  tau.bforest <- 1/sd.bforest^2
  mu.bforest2 ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.bforest2 ~ dt(0, 1, 1)T(0,)
  tau.bforest2 <- 1/sd.bforest2^2

##for detection
  mu.a0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.a0 ~ dt(0, 1, 1)T(0,)
  tau.a0 <- 1/sd.a0^2

  mu.atrail ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.atrail ~ dt(0, 1, 1)T(0,)
  tau.atrail <- 1/sd.atrail^2

  rho ~ dunif(-1, 1)
  tau.eta <- tau.a0/(1 - rho^2)

  # Derived quantities
  for(i in 1:nSites) {
  Nsite[i] <- sum(z[i,]) #richness per site
  }
  N <- sum(w)                 # Total metacommunity size

}

